; Raise the V8 old-space cap for the Vitest gate.
;
; MEASURED, not guessed: the full suite with coverage peaks at 4576 MB RSS in
; its largest process, and node's default cap on this toolchain is 4288 MB. So
; the gate died at the ceiling as exit 134 (SIGABRT from V8's OOM handler) with
; NO summary block at all, which reads as green to anything grepping for a
; failure count.
;
; THE VALUE IS BOUNDED BY THE SMALLEST MACHINE THAT READS THIS FILE, which is
; Cloud Build's E2_HIGHCPU_8 (8 vCPU, 8 GB RAM; cloudbuild-staging.yaml:989,
; cloudbuild-prod.yaml:309, cloudbuild-assessment-lifecycle.yaml:270), NOT a
; 32 GB laptop. A cap above the machine's RAM would be a REGRESSION: V8 would
; allocate past physical memory and the kernel OOM killer would SIGKILL it
; (exit 137, no V8 message) where today it fails legibly. 6144 clears the
; measured 4576 by 1568 MB and leaves ~2 GB on an 8 GB worker.
;
; npm applies this to every script and `npx` run in this directory, so the
; C-GATE one-command gate is unchanged and vitest.config.ts is untouched. Note
; it also governs the `npm ci` on cloudbuild-staging.yaml:140, not just vitest.
node-options=--max-old-space-size=6144
